# Standard Git workflow (Stackward)

**This is the default for every task.** No exceptions unless the user explicitly says otherwise.

## Definition of done

Work is **not complete** until:

1. Changes are on a **feature branch** (never directly on `main`)
2. The branch is **pushed** to `origin`
3. A **draft PR** against `main` exists
4. **alexseymer** is requested as reviewer (or @mentioned if the API blocks assignment)

Do not push feature commits to `main`. Do not mark tasks finished without an open PR.

## Standard flow

```text
main → feature branch → commit → push → draft PR → request review from alexseymer
```

1. Branch from latest `main`: `cursor/<short-description>`
2. Implement and commit on the branch
3. `git push -u origin <branch>`
4. Open draft PR against `main`
5. Assign reviewer **alexseymer** (required for GitHub push notifications)

## Creating PRs

```bash
gh pr create \
  --base main \
  --head <branch> \
  --title "<title>" \
  --body "<body>" \
  --draft \
  --reviewer alexseymer
```

Or `ManagePullRequest` with `create_pr`, then:

```bash
gh pr edit <number> --add-reviewer alexseymer
```

If reviewer assignment fails (integration token), post a PR comment:

```text
@alexseymer — Review requested.
```

## Merge policy

- **Do not merge PRs** unless the user explicitly asks
- User reviews in the GitHub app and merges when ready

## Do not

- `git push origin main` for feature work
- Skip the PR step because changes are “small” or “already discussed”
- Skip reviewer assignment / @alexseymer mention
- Create retrospective PRs unless the user asks
